:: Mason Walk Refuse
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>

<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"폐를 끼치고 싶지 않아요." 당신은 말한다. "괜찮을 거예요."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite">>
	"Thank you, but I'll manage," you say. "I know the way."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"It's alright," you say. "You don't need to trouble yourself over me."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
	"I'll survive the spooky little walk," you say. "Thank you, though."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"제가 어둠을 무서워하는 것처럼 보이나요?" 당신은 묻는다. "괜찮을 거예요."
<<else>>
	"괜찮아요." 당신은 말한다. "숲길은 잘 알아요."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Mason lingers a moment as though still deciding whether to argue, but finally nods. "If you're sure. Be careful." <<He>> dries <<himself>> with a towel as <<he>> heads back into the forest.
<br><br>

